# Tiered register allocation (shed / borrow / direct-fallback)
#
# rvv_matmul_engine_t::configure() allocates its general-purpose scratch
# registers through a tiered search: try everything at full cost with B
# addressed via `pivot`, shed registers (outermost bookkeeping first, the
# innermost K-loop's own re-arm register last) if that doesn't fit, then
# retry the whole ladder with B via `direct` if shedding still isn't enough.
# max_int_regs artificially caps the int register pool so that search is
# actually forced into specific rungs, rather than trivially succeeding at
# level 0 the way every shape in the other harness files does with the
# default ~24-register pool.
# The three operand pointers are loaded into pool registers (from the args
# structure), so each cap includes those three.
--reset
--max_int_regs=10
64x128x32_n"register_tight_tile_base_demotion"

--reset
--transB=1 --max_int_regs=11
64x128x32_n"register_tight_direct_fallback"

--reset
--transA=1 --transB=1 --max_int_regs=12
64x128x32_n"register_tight_transab_direct_fallback"
